Third-party components invoked by KaggleUI, and their licenses.

Both are driven strictly as subprocesses, in isolated environments. KaggleUI never imports,
vendors, links against, or distributes their source; they remain separate works and are
installed only when the user enables the feature that needs them.

Heretic — https://github.com/p-e-w/heretic
  License: AGPL-3.0
  Used by: the abliteration / behavior-edit stage (kaggleui/catalog/abliterate_worker.py,
  kaggleui/ml/edit.py), launched as a child process with an isolated `uv` environment.

mergekit — https://github.com/arcee-ai/mergekit
  License: LGPL-3.0
  Used by: model merge/convert jobs (kaggleui/ml/conversion.py) in the isolated training venv,
  invoked through its command line, never imported.

llama.cpp — https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
  License: MIT
  Used by: llama-server, llama-quantize, llama-imatrix, llama-gguf-split binaries downloaded
  from the pinned release (kaggleui/engines/llamacpp_release.py), plus llama-swap
  (https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap, MIT).

trl, peft, transformers, accelerate, datasets, bitsandbytes
  Licenses: Apache-2.0 (trl, peft, transformers, datasets), Apache-2.0 (accelerate),
  MIT (bitsandbytes)
  Used by: LoRA/QLoRA training inside the isolated training venv.
